idioelectric.d:
a. Electric by virtue of its own peculiar properties;
   capable of becoming electrified by friction; -- opposed to anelectric.
n. An idioelectric substance.

impartible.d:
a. Capable of being imparted or communicated.
a. Not partible; not subject to partition; indivisible;
   as, an impartible estate.

impolicy.d:
n. The quality of being impolitic; inexpedience;
   unsuitableness to the end proposed; bads policy; as, the impolicy of
   fraud.
